---
import PageIntro from "../components/page/PageIntro.astro";
import SceneFigure from "../components/atmosphere/SceneFigure.astro";
import withheldReflection from "../assets/scenery/withheld-reflection.png";
import { pageMetadata } from "../config/pageMetadata";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBasePath } from "../lib/routing";
import "../styles/atmosphere-content.css";

const metadata = pageMetadata.about;
---

<BaseLayout {...metadata}>
  <article class="page about-page atmospheric-page">
    <div class="atmospheric-about-grid">
      <div class="atmospheric-about-copy">
        <PageIntro
          headerClass="about-page__header atmospheric-page-intro"
          eyebrow="Professional profile"
          title="About"
        >
          I’m {siteConfig.name}, a {siteConfig.role}. This page will provide a
          concise introduction to my professional background, engineering
          approach, and the work represented throughout this portfolio.
        </PageIntro>

        <section class="about-page__status atmospheric-content-block">
          <p class="atmospheric-section-number">01 / Introductions</p>
          <h2>Who is Zeus?</h2>

          <p>
            It's me. I'm Zeus. I'm a developer passionate about finding
            solutions, optimizing workflows and building better channels for us
            all to work and live within. I think we'd work really well together.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="about-page__scope atmospheric-content-block">
          <h2>What this page will cover</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>My professional background and progression</li>
            <li>My approach to engineering and technical problem-solving</li>
            <li>
              The principles that guide the work presented in this portfolio
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="about-page__status atmospheric-content-block">
          <p class="atmospheric-section-number">02 / My background</p>
          <h2>Where did he come from?</h2>

          <p>I came from passion.</p>
          <p>
            I was always interested in tech and developing. At just 12 years old
            I was developing Minecraft mods, at 10 I was playing with Python
            injectors built by others on video games I loved and at 9 I was
            playing with HTML and CSS. I've always loved hardware and software.
          </p>
          <p>
            My career was pretty simple, started off with a development
            bootcamp, got into General Motors, then into a software insurance
            company named Finys. At General Motors at first I helped with
            pipeline updates for their CI and BV pipelines, then I moved onto
            platform tools like their Visual Site Regression tool. Finys had
            much of the same, platform tools and pipelines.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="about-page__status atmospheric-content-block">
          <p class="atmospheric-section-number">03 / Technical Philosophy</p>
          <h2>What rules decide what you build?</h2>

          <h3>Think it through and be thorough.</h3>
          <p>
            The last thing anyone wants to accumulate is tech debt from poorly
            decided "solutions". Bandaid solutions are unnacceptable, and if a
            situation can't be fixed right away, coordination should be in place
            to establish the proper means of doing so.
          </p>
          <h3>Take accountability and don't be afraid to speak up.</h3>
          <p>
            Sometimes things go wrong, and when they do, it's okay to admit to
            it and formulate a plan to fix it. It's important to step up and
            establish ways to do things. It's important to take initiative and
            ownership on projects and work.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="about-page__status atmospheric-content-block">
          <p class="atmospheric-section-number">04 / Portfolio Philosophy</p>
          <h2>Why does your portfolio look like this?</h2>
          <p>
            I'm a huge horror and satire fan. I was deeply inspired by the works
            of David Lynch, Akira Yamaoka and of course, GTA. A secret, hidden
            portion of my site is actually formulated to work like the internet
            accessible in GTA 4 and GTA 5, satire that serves almost like
            political commentary. It's advocacy for data privacy and poking fun
            at the people behind it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="about-page__next-steps atmospheric-content-block">
          <h2>Continue exploring</h2>

          <ul class="page-actions atmospheric-actions">
            <li>
              <a href={withBasePath("/resume", import.meta.env.BASE_URL)}
                >View my resume</a
              >
            </li>

            <li>
              <a href={withBasePath("/work", import.meta.env.BASE_URL)}
                >View selected work</a
              >
            </li>

            <li>
              <a href={withBasePath("/contact", import.meta.env.BASE_URL)}
                >Contact me</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>

      <SceneFigure
        image={withheldReflection}
        alt="An empty chair faces a wall mirror whose reflection shows a different, unoccupied corridor."
        caption="There is always more to know."
        number="02"
        variant="interior"
      />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
